{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548139-losing-magic-tools","id":1548139,"title":"Losing magic tools","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-03T05:53:17-08:00","id":1548139,"title":"Losing magic tools","content":"Im really not stisfied withn how originally the loosing of tools mechanic is described in mage. Most of the time the characters uste those same 3-4 tools all the time so losing them makes no difference.<br /> Therefore do you have any fun and better mechanics i could implement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T14:21:07-08:00","id":1548154,"title":"","content":"A house rule I've used is to change it from &quot;which Instruments can you do away with?&quot; to &quot;which Effects can do away with Instruments?&quot; Keeping the mystics vs. technomancy divide, a mystic can dispense with Instruments if she has twice as much Arete as the highest Sphere required for the Effect; and a technomancer can dispense with Instruments if his Arete is 5 higher than the highest Sphere required. So a rank 1 Effect can dispense with Instruments at Arete 2 (for a mystic) or Arete 6 (for a technomancer); a rank 2 Effect can dispense with instruments at Arete 4 or 7; a rank 3 Effect can be performed without Instruments at Arete 6 or 8; for a rank 4 Effect, it's 8 or 9; and for a Rank 5 Effect, it's 10. <br /> <br /> Note that this doesn't play well with Archspheres as defined in <b>Horizon: Stronghold of Hope</b> or <b>Masters of the Art</b>; but I prefer to define Archspheres in a manner similar to how they're done in <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/446015/prism-of-focus\" target=\"_blank\">Prism of Focus</a>, where dots after the fifth don't unlock new Effects unavailable at lower dots but instead provide you with ways to enhance the Effects already unlocked. So once you reach Arete 10 and have gained the ability to perform rank 5 Effects without Instruments, you're able to perform <i>any</i> Effect without Instruments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T14:30:41-08:00","id":1548156,"title":"","content":"It's hard to know what to suggest because your complaint is kinda vague?<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that you still benefit from instruments if you &quot;lose&quot; them. What you lose is the requirement to have them available to cast your magic. It's a benefit that makes catching mages off-guard (a default tactic since mages can do so much when prepared) harder as they grow in Arete. I guess that's a bit underwhelming, but without a serious overhaul of how things work, I'm not sure you can make something more impactful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-04T00:08:41-08:00","id":1548176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548139-losing-magic-tools?p=1548156#post1548156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's hard to know what to suggest because your complaint is kinda vague?<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that you still benefit from instruments if you &quot;lose&quot; them. What you lose is the requirement to have them available to cast your magic. It's a benefit that makes catching mages off-guard (a default tactic since mages can do so much when prepared) harder as they grow in Arete. I guess that's a bit underwhelming, but without a serious overhaul of how things work, I'm not sure you can make something more impactful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats exactly the point. You cant really know if a new spell needed the tool you have thrown away or not, therefore its a bad mechanic. As for the past effects it forces to keep rotes what is just busy work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-04T03:31:57-08:00","id":1548180,"title":"","content":"Something else I've considered is to tie the number of Instruments you need for an Effect to the number of successes you need to pull off the Effect. From one Instrument for Effects requiring a single success to seven Instruments for Effects requiring 20+ successes, the bigger the Effect that you attempt the more instrumentation you need to make it work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-04T04:21:27-08:00","id":1548181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548139-losing-magic-tools?p=1548176#post1548176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats exactly the point. You cant really know if a new spell needed the tool you have thrown away or not, therefore its a bad mechanic. As for the past effects it forces to keep rotes what is just busy work.</div> </div> </div> </div>This... doesn't make much sense. You don't &quot;throw away&quot; tools, because they're still useful to your mage. The wording of the text might not be great, but in D&amp;D terms, you're a Fighter that slowly builds up groups of weapons that they can draw as a free action and never be disarmed while wielding, until they basically always have whatever weapons they want and nobody can stop them from at least having them. You also don't lose access to rotes if you don't have to use a specific instrument any more.<br /> <br /> The lose of Instrument requirements isn't, in and of itself, a bad mechanic. It's framed messily, and it depends on a part of the system that's always been incredibly vague; leaving it extremely variable in impact based on group play style.<br /> <br /> Dataweaver is pointing out the real area of the system that's lacking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-04T05:36:10-08:00","id":1548184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548139-losing-magic-tools?p=1548181#post1548181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This... doesn't make much sense. You don't &quot;throw away&quot; tools, because they're still useful to your mage. The wording of the text might not be great, but in D&amp;D terms, you're a Fighter that slowly builds up groups of weapons that they can draw as a free action and never be disarmed while wielding, until they basically always have whatever weapons they want and nobody can stop them from at least having them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you are making no sesne. There is no information of using tools for free. Only that you dont have to use it anymore and its sugested you should start with those you do not use that often.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-04T06:19:27-08:00","id":1548185,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that Instruments (formerly known as &quot;foci&quot;) used to be tied to Spheres; and as such, &quot;losing&quot; an Instrument was equivalent to picking a Sphere that no longer needed an Instrument. You still see vestiges of this in M20 where it gets into Personalized and Unique Instruments, which are still tied to Spheres: everyone gets a Personalized Instrument for their Affinity Sphere, and any mage can declare another Instrument to be Unique, binding it to one Sphere and saying that the mage can only work Effects involving that Sphere using that exact Instrument. It wouldn't be all that hard to put that back into place for Common Instruments, too: the main change would be to go back to the idea that you chose Spheres where the associated Instruments become optional, and mystics start doing this at Arete 2. <br /> <br /> The catch to this approach is that it assumes that the mage will assign one Instrument to each and every Sphere, and that he'll end up with dots in every Sphere. The reality is that most mages only use three or four Sphere; so they end up not needing any Instruments for anything they do well before hitting Arete 9. Exactly the same problem <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28439\" data-vbnamecard=\"28439\">quelsec</a> mentioned at the start of this topic. In short, the problem isn't anything new; it's been around in some form or another since the first edition of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-04T10:57:29-08:00","id":1548192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548139-losing-magic-tools?p=1548184#post1548184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now you are making no sesne. There is no information of using tools for free. Only that you dont have to use it anymore and its sugested you should start with those you do not use that often.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an analogy, I'm aware it's imperfect. Allow me to expand a bit:<br /> <br /> There's a difference between a Fighter that has a small arsenal of always available normal weapons, and a Fighter using a +1 long sword. Never having to worry about being caught without your weapons isn't the same as having the best weapon.<br /> <br /> A mage that's overcome their most used instruments has achieved the flexibility of the &quot;always armed&quot; Fighter, but not the power of one with the magical sword; if you want the magical sword you still need to bring it with you. A mage that &quot;throws away&quot; all their instruments is the same as a Fighter that throws away their +1 sword because they can have a normal sword whenever they want it... it's not really something that makes sense in-universe or mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}